<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 75,170 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 75,170 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 75,170 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Thursday compared to 84,785 tonnes in the same period on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Thursday    April 23</p>
<p>    Export cargo		16,035	 7,140</p>
<p>    Import cargo		59,135	77,645</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, six ships sailed and two berthed. In the next 24 hours, four are expected to sail and 12 are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	Tonnes/TEUs  Ship			Berthing</p>
<p>Crude oil	    70,000	 Stavros-I		 24/4</p>
<p>Palm oil		6,200	 Wawasan Megah	   25/4</p>
<p>Palm oil		8,600	 Wawasan Courage	 25/4</p>
<p>Rock phosphate     22,000	 Artemis-II		25/4</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
